-- title:
--   Hyperbolic norm class of an upper-triangular δ
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ and $L$ be fields with $L$ an $F$-algebra that is finite-dimensional and Galois over $F$, and let $\sigma$ be an $F$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_F(L)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is generated by $\sigma$). Let $\delta \in GL_2(L)$ have vanishing lower-left entry, $\delta_{10} = 0$. Here $GL_2(L)$ carries the $\sigma$-conjugacy equivalence $\delta_1 \sim \delta_2 \iff \delta_2 = k^{-1}\delta_1\,\sigma(k)$ for some $k \in GL_2(L)$ ($\sigma$ acting entrywise), [`LT.TwistedNorm.SigmaConjClasses.mk σ δ`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L718) is the class of $\delta$ for this relation, and [`LT.TwistedNorm.normClassMap hgen`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L766) sends such a class to the $GL_2(F)$-conjugacy class of a representative chosen by `exists_map_eq_conj_sigmaNormPow`, that is, of an element of $GL_2(F)$ attached to the $\sigma$-norm of $\delta$, this class being independent of the representative of the $\sigma$-conjugacy class. The assertion is the equivalence: there exists $\gamma \in GL_2(F)$ whose characteristic polynomial factors as $(X - a)(X - b)$ with $a \neq b$ in $F$ (membership in [`AutomorphicForm.hyperbolicCell F`](def/AutomorphicForm_GL2ConjugacyCells.html#L32)) and whose conjugacy class is the norm class of the $\sigma$-conjugacy class of $\delta$, if and only if $N_{L/F}(\delta_{00}/\delta_{11}) \neq 1$, the norm being `Algebra.norm F`.
--
--   This is the criterion, in the geometric side of the twisted trace formula for $GL_2$ over a cyclic extension $L/F$, identifying which upper-triangular $\delta$ have norm class of hyperbolic (regular split) type rather than central type. It is used in the comparisons of truncated integrals of automorphic forms against constant terms over the hyperbolic and unipotent cells.
-- source:
